+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Customers can create, pay, and cancel orders, and administrators can manage coupons, but there is no way to actually redeem a coupon against an order. The `orders.discount_cents`, `orders.final_amount_cents`, `orders.coupon_code` columns and the `coupon_redemptions` table already exist but are never written. This change adds the missing redemption step so a customer can apply one coupon to a pending order and have the payable amount drop accordingly.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": "..." }`.
+- On success, return HTTP 200 with the updated order, in exactly the same shape as `GET /orders/:id`.
+- Validate the request, order, and coupon in the fixed order defined by the task error table, returning the existing `{ error: { code, message } }` shape with the specified status codes.
+- Compute the discount (FIXED / PERCENT, with cap and floor at zero) from the injected `Clock`.
+- Persist all success-side writes (order update, redemption row, `used_count` increment) atomically in a single transaction; a rejection or failure leaves the database unchanged.
+- Add tests covering the acceptance criteria; no schema, dependency, or existing-test changes.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `coupon-redemption`: Redeeming a coupon against a pending order — request normalization, validation ordering and error codes, discount computation, atomic persistence, and the response contract.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+<!-- None: there are no existing specs in this project. -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- New route: `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`.
+- New service logic in `src/services/orderService.ts` (or a dedicated service) implementing the rules; `CouponService`/`OrderService` wiring may be extended.
+- New repository SQL in `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts` and `src/repositories/couponRepository.ts` (transactional order update, redemption insert, `used_count` increment).
+- `src/app.ts` wiring if a new service/dependency is introduced.
+- New tests under `tests/`.
+- No changes to the database schema, no new dependencies, no changes to existing tests.
