+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Persistence layer
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents, createdAt)` that updates the order (`discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents`, `coupon_code`), inserts one `coupon_redemptions` row, and increments `coupons.used_count`, all inside a single `BEGIN`/`COMMIT` with `ROLLBACK` and rethrow on error. Verify with a repository-level test that all three writes are visible after success and that an induced failure leaves the database unchanged.
+
+## 2. Service layer
+
+- [x] 2.1 Inject `CouponRepository` into `OrderService` and update `createApp` wiring in `src/app.ts`. Verify `npm run build` passes and the existing `npm test` suite still passes unchanged.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)`: normalize the code (trim then uppercase), then check conditions in the required precedence order (`INVALID_REQUEST` → `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` → `ORDER_NOT_PENDING` → `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED` → `COUPON_NOT_FOUND` → `COUPON_INACTIVE` → `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID`/`COUPON_EXPIRED` → `COUPON_USAGE_EXHAUSTED` → `MINIMUM_NOT_MET`), reading `now` from the injected Clock. Verify with tests asserting each status/code and that every rejection leaves the database unchanged.
+- [x] 2.3 Implement discount computation and persistence: FIXED → `value`; PERCENT → `floor(amount * value / 100)`; apply `maxDiscountCents` cap when non-null; clamp to `amount`; `final = amount - discount`; store the normalized uppercase code. Verify tests covering AC-01–AC-06 and AC-10 (`" save20 "` matches `SAVE20`).
+
+## 3. HTTP route
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`, delegating to the service after `parseId`. Verify integration tests: HTTP 200 body equals `GET /orders/:id` (AC-14), second use returns 409 `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED` with amounts unchanged (AC-08), and success increments `GET /coupons/:code` `usedCount` and adds a `coupon_redemptions` row (AC-09).
+
+## 4. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build` and `npm test`; confirm both pass and that no existing test file was modified.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after the implementation is reviewed and accepted.
